{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01463",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.22,
      "end_seconds": 6.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "Hi, doctor, I came as soon as they called me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.09,
      "end_seconds": 11.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 11.82,
      "end_seconds": 14.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Doctor, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.63,
      "end_seconds": 25.61,
      "duration_seconds": 8.98,
      "text": "Honestly, it's the room spinning when I turn over in bed, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.17,
      "end_seconds": 30.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.19,
      "end_seconds": 39.79,
      "duration_seconds": 7.6,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, I'd say once or twice a day. I'd call it severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.93,
      "end_seconds": 46.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Okay, is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.48,
      "end_seconds": 60.52,
      "duration_seconds": 12.04,
      "text": "Being unsteady for a few minutes goes along with it, most of the time. The being unsteady for a few minutes? That's been for four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.31,
      "end_seconds": 65.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.39,
      "end_seconds": 74.29,
      "duration_seconds": 6.9,
      "text": "I'd call it moderate. I'd been feeling sick, but that went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.49,
      "end_seconds": 90.71,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "Have you noticed ringing in the ear, weakness or double vision?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.71,
      "end_seconds": 97.37,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "No, no ringing in the ear, weakness or double vision."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.22,
      "end_seconds": 101.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Okay, any hearing loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.42,
      "end_seconds": 108.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "No hearing loss, thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.31,
      "end_seconds": 114.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "On the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.06,
      "end_seconds": 118.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.41,
      "end_seconds": 121.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "So, how's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.33,
      "end_seconds": 124.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "Breathing's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.11,
      "end_seconds": 129.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.18,
      "end_seconds": 136.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.02,
      "text": "My mother had a stroke. My mother has an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.49,
      "end_seconds": 140.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.81,
      "end_seconds": 152.52,
      "duration_seconds": 11.71,
      "text": "Yes, you know, I had my septum straightened, in my thirties. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.11,
      "end_seconds": 156.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.39,
      "end_seconds": 170.65,
      "duration_seconds": 12.26,
      "text": "Hmm, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.73,
      "end_seconds": 177.78,
      "duration_seconds": 6.05,
      "text": "Right, what about your medical history? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.82,
      "end_seconds": 182.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "I've had gout, yes. Yes, depression."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.02,
      "end_seconds": 185.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Okay, what else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.41,
      "end_seconds": 188.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Yes, high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.95,
      "end_seconds": 190.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "Any other things?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.9,
      "end_seconds": 204.03,
      "duration_seconds": 9.13,
      "text": "Okay, I can see depression in your file as well. Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.09,
      "end_seconds": 217.08,
      "duration_seconds": 10.99,
      "text": "I swim twice a week. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.17,
      "end_seconds": 222.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.68,
      "end_seconds": 230.94,
      "duration_seconds": 8.26,
      "text": "I'm on allopurinol, 100 milligrams, once a day. It's fluoxetine, 20 milligrams, every morning for my mood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.97,
      "end_seconds": 236.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Since when have you been taking it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.16,
      "end_seconds": 245.97,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "About a month now. I take simvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night for my cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.75,
      "end_seconds": 249.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.7,
      "end_seconds": 259.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.12,
      "end_seconds": 285.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.88,
      "text": "Okay: heart rate 70, respiratory rate 17, BP is 121 over 81."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.91,
      "end_seconds": 291.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Alright, over here please and I'll take a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.22,
      "end_seconds": 294.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.33,
      "end_seconds": 316.22,
      "duration_seconds": 7.89,
      "text": "When I tip you back, the eyes flick for about twenty seconds, and the hearing is normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.43,
      "end_seconds": 323.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "All finished, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.14,
      "end_seconds": 348.89,
      "duration_seconds": 10.75,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, I'd lean towards benign positional vertigo. A vestibular neuritis is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.12,
      "end_seconds": 389.14,
      "duration_seconds": 22.02,
      "text": "I'll do a repositioning manoeuvre now and show you exercises for home. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 390.33,
      "end_seconds": 392.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Thank you, that's clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 393.15,
      "end_seconds": 401.25,
      "duration_seconds": 8.1,
      "text": "We'll catch up in two weeks. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 402.78,
      "end_seconds": 404.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Thank you, that's helpful."
    }
  ]
}